</script>

# Orbling

Shows an orb with a face that tells the user what an AI assistant is doing, such as thinking, reading, typing, working, or asking a question. Each mood plays its own CSS animation, the palette derives from one theme color, and the `OrblingStatus` part pairs a small orb with a shimmering label for chat status lines. Every part holds still when the user prefers reduced motion, and the component needs no WebGL or extra packages.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Orbling } from "#lib/components/ui/orbling/index.js";
</script>

<Orbling mood="thinking" size="lg" />
```

## Installation

Run the command below to add the component to `src/lib/components/ui/orbling`.

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/orbling.json
```

## Moods

Set `mood` to `idle`, `thinking`, `reading`, `typing`, `working`, `asking`, `waiting`, `watching`, `surprised`, `sleepy`, or `error`. The default is `idle`, a new mood starts its animation from the beginning, and `watching` turns the eyes toward the pointer.

<Demo section="moods" />

- Use `thinking` while the assistant works out an answer
- Use `reading` while it reads pages, files, or results
- Use `typing` while it writes the reply
- Use `working` while a tool or task runs
- Use `asking` when it asks the user a question, then `waiting` until the user answers
- Use `watching` for an empty state that waits on the user
- Use `error` when something fails

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Orbling mood="working" />
```

## Variants

Set `variant` to `default`, `secondary`, or `destructive`. The default variant is blue from `--chart-1`, `secondary` is grey from `--muted-foreground`, and `destructive` is red from `--destructive`.

<Demo section="variants" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Orbling variant="secondary" />
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`, which sets a diameter of 16, 32, 72, or 120 pixels. The default is `md`.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Orbling size="sm" />
```

## Colors

Set `--orbling-color` to change the base color. The orb keeps the lightness of its original palette and takes the hue and chroma of the color you set, so any theme token works.

<Demo section="colors" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Orbling style="--orbling-color: var(--chart-3)" />
```

## Status

Use `OrblingStatus` for a status line in a chat. It shows a 16 pixel orb beside the mood label, such as "Thinking…", uses `role="status"` so screen readers announce changes, and takes `mood`, `variant`, `size`, and a `label` that replaces the default text.

<Demo section="status" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { OrblingStatus } from "#lib/components/ui/orbling/index.js";
</script>

<OrblingStatus mood="reading" label="Reading the docs…" />
```

## Accessibility

The orb is decorative by default, so screen readers skip it. Set `label` when the orb carries meaning, which gives it `role="img"` and an accessible name.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Orbling mood="thinking" label="Assistant is thinking" />
```

## API

The `Orbling` and `OrblingStatus` props extend the native `span` attributes, and extra attributes pass through to the root. The package also exports `MOODS`, which maps each mood to its label, and `MOOD_NAMES`, which lists every mood.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompProps<"span"> {
	/** What the assistant is doing; defaults to `idle` */
	mood?: Mood;
	/** Orb colors: `default` is blue from `--chart-1`, `secondary` is grey, and `destructive` is red; `--orbling-color` overrides the base color */
	variant?: "default" | "secondary" | "destructive";
	/** Orb diameter on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Accessible name; without it screen readers skip the orb */
	label?: string;
}

interface StatusProps extends CompProps<"span"> {
	/** What the assistant is doing; defaults to `idle` */
	mood?: Mood;
	/** Orb colors, as on `Orbling` */
	variant?: "default" | "secondary" | "destructive";
	/** Label text and gap on the shared scale; defaults to `sm` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Status text; defaults to the mood label, such as "Thinking…" */
	label?: string;
}
```

## Credits

Orbling is a Svelte port of [orbling](https://orbling.vercel.app) by Timotej Kochjar, released under the MIT License. The original React component and its source live at [github.com/kochjar/orbling](https://github.com/kochjar/orbling). This port keeps its moods and motion, replaces the WebGL heat shader with the original's CSS glow, and derives the palette from theme tokens.
